@0    = ~We're here. This is the place I spoke of.~
@1    = ~This place is infested with filth and webs. Do whatever you must swiftly so we may leave.~
@2    = ~Why must we be in a place such as this, <CHARNAME>? For the sake of this ghost?~
@3    = ~We're here because I say so, Anomen. Anyways, Will... what now?~
@4    = ~What's so special about this place?~
@5    = ~Here? Really? Uhm, are you sure about that?~
@6    = ~Right. So, why are we here?~
@7    = ~This is the place where I died... as well as the place to which I'm bound. But the restoration of the Visionhive has given me enough power to influence this bond. I may untie my spirit partially... enough to travel with you.~
@8    = ~He... he really died in this sad and quiet place? How terrible... he must have felt so lonely.~
@9    = ~Yes, I agree it's sad, Aerie, but regardless, we should allow Will to do what he must. Do you need help?~
@10   = ~I understand. Do what you must, Will, so we may begin our adventures together.~
@11   = ~Will you need some time to do... this thing you need to do?~
@12   = ~Do you need me to do anything to aid you?~
@13   = ~I've got everything I need. It will only take a minute.~
@14   = ~There... it's done.~
@15   = ~Are you feeling alright?~
@16   = ~What did you do?~
@17   = ~Yes... yes, I'm fine.~
@18   = ~Are you sure about that? If you need some time to recover...~
@19   = ~As I said before, I needed to influence the power that bound me to this place. This... place is important to me. After all, I did pass away here. Now, though...~
@20   = ~I should be able to come and go as I wish. If I tried before performing the rite, my spirit would be overwhelmed, destroyed and then recreated here. This... place serves as a dome for my spirit. I needed to take a piece of my remains and tie it to this amulet, so that it might maintain my shape.~
@21   = ~There is something else you should know. If I fall in battle, your magic won't be able to resurrect me. I am but a spirit, after all. But instead of passing on, I will return here... eventually. You may return here to find me. I think that was the last important thing.~
@22   = ~I won't lie to you - it's a strange feeling to leave. The world is open to me now, but so much time has passed since I've looked upon anything outside of these grounds. But... I'm ready to go.~
@23   = ~I'm glad to hear it. Come, we should get going.~
@24   = ~Now's your chance, Will. There's no place for fear. You are now the freest you've been since your dead. Everything will be just fine.~
@25   = ~Enough babbling. Just get in line so we may move on. We've got a lot of work to do.~
@26   = ~Right. Lead on, and I'll be right behind you.~
@27   = ~Yes, I know. What I'm feeling is not fear. Perhaps a bit of both curiosity and concern, but not fear. Let's go.~
@28   = ~Just quiet yourself and lead us.~
@29   = ~What... what is this place...?~
@30   = ~We're in Athkatla. These are the City Gates.~
@31   = ~We're in Athkatla. This is the Docks district.~
@32   = ~We're in Athkatla. This is the Slums district.~
@33   = ~We're in Athkatla. This is the Bridge district.~
@34   = ~We're in Athkatla. And that's the Waukeen's Promenade.~
@35   = ~We're in Athkatla. This is the Temple district.~
@36   = ~We're in Athkatla. This is the Government district.~
@37   = ~We're in Athkatla. And that's the western part of the Government district.~
@38   = ~That's Trademeet. The City of Merchant's Peace. Although it hasn't been very peaceful lately.~
@39   = ~What do you mean?~
@40   = ~We don't have time for this. Let's move on.~
@41   = ~This place. Where is this... where are we? Does this place have a name?~
@42   = ~We don't have time for this. Let's move on, Will.~
@43   = ~I remember this city being much smaller when I was still alive. It was mostl humans that walked the streets, but now - elves, dwarves, even gnomes... so many people, and the architecture - it's all changed greatly as well. Nothing's the same to the place I remember.~
@44   = ~I suppose that place was just an echo of what it is now.~
@45   = ~So I'm guessing you don't like the way it looks now?~
@46   = ~Heh. I could mistake you for a bard or storyteller with your choice of metaphors.~
@47   = ~I'm afraid now's no time to be discussing cities and their infrastructure. Let's get moving, Will.~
@48   = ~I didn't say that. This city, and the one from long ago - they are different places. Death has taught me that a place is determined by the moment in time that it exists in. I remember a place only half as big as where we are now, with different people and different laws.~
@49   = ~The past Athkatla is another place altogether. Yours... this one that we can see now is a place of a wholly different culture.~
@50   = ~The past Trademeet was different. Maybe only half as big, and much more... raw. There were less people, though still many merchants. And I remember many more trees surrounding the town as well.~
@51   = ~I doubt I'd enjoy it. I love listening to tales, but telling them... no, I'm no entertainer. And I doubt an undead bard would attract many listeners.~
@52   = ~Anyways, about the city... Athkatla was a different place in the time that I was alive. Yours... this one that we can see now is a place of a wholly different culture.~
@53   = ~But speaking about the city - when I was alive, Trademeet was different. It was half as big, much more... raw. There were less people, but still many merchants. There were more trees aroud the city, too.~
@54   = ~I wonder... are many other cities just the same as this as well?~
@55   = ~Well, Baldur's Gate was quite big. I spent some time there before I was captured by Irenicus.~
@56   = ~I think it would depend on the region. The wealthy places would change more than the poor ones. But I suppose they would all change, at least a little.~
@57   = ~I can't really say. I'm not all that familiar with other cities.~
@58   = ~Baldur's Gate, hmm? I think I've heard of it. The great city surrounded by the wall that Balduran himself ordered to be built at the river Chionthar, right? I've never been there, though.~
@59   = ~I apologize. That wasn't a very smart question to ask. Of course every city would change. It's been many long years since...~
@60   = ~...~
@61   = ~My father was a merchant. I think that's the reason the picture of the city struck me so soundly. All these people living their lives buying, selling, spending their earnings in the local taverns... Father used to say: "Money is the lifeblood of the city, and just like blood - it rushes and never slows down.~
@62   = ~You and your father must have gotten along well. Did you like each other well?~
@63   = ~Hmm, well, I think there are times when people will spend less of their gold, but I get what he's trying to say.~
@64   = ~That's all very nice, but we really should be moving on.~
@65   = ~Did your father teach you a lot about trade?~
@66   = ~We loved each other... most of the time, anyways. He didn't want me to leave, and it wasn't just so I could take over the family business. I think he knew... knew there was something that always made me think, and wouldn't let me let my guard down. He was concerned for me.~
@67   = ~He thought I would always need him, and... perhaps he was right. Later in my life, there were many times where I wished he could help me. But he was already gone... no, *I* was gone. I was the one who created the distance between us.~
@68   = ~Of course. People would treasure onto their gold in harsh times. My father knew that. It was simply a saying he was fond of. I think he enjoyed both the earning and spending of money. He found peace in buying goods to make sure our family felt safe and well at home.~
@69   = ~No, not really. I usually just observed him. But he knew I would choose to learn the trade myself anyway, if it interested me enough. Father cared about me. He didn't want me to leave, and it wasn't just so I could take over the family business. I think he knew... knew there was something that always made me think, and wouldn't let me let my guard down. He was concerned for me.~
@70   = ~All things considered though, my father was a fine man. Perhaps it was a mistake for me to hide my thoughts from him. When I grew older, we would talk even less than usual. I think that must have hurt him.~
@71   = ~What about your mother?~
@72   = ~You were lucky to have a loving father. Why would you not talk to him?~
@73   = ~That's enough, Will. I think we should get moving.~
@74   = ~She was a novelist, but she didn't write many books. None of them were very long either, but I personally liked them. Father helped her publish her stories. All of them were fictional, but... (smile) well, maybe her tales weren't that disconnected with reality after all. Now I know that.~
@75   = ~I know that.~
@76   = ~Anyways, I think we should move on. We're not here to discuss this, but still... thank you. I think I needed to talk about it.~
@77   = ~Fine.~
@78   = ~I've been thinking about my father a lot, ever since we last talked... thinking about how I left him and my mother. I wonder what happened to them after I left. I may have done a great injustice, leaving them and never going back.~
@79   = ~It might have been, indeed, but we all make mistakes.~
@80   = ~You did what you wanted to do. You heard your calling and then you left. We all do it someday, only under different circumstances.~
@81   = ~This is your own busines, Will. I'd rather you not discuss it with me.~
@82   = ~Perhaps you're right...~
@83   = ~Circumstances... they're always the most important part. They might cause hurt, destruction... or raise hope.~
@84   = ~The past is too far gone, though. Whatever might have happened is long done. I've considered asking the spirits of what fates befell them, but even if I knew, I wouldn't be able to undo it. So I never did, and I doubt I ever will.~
@85   = ~I'm sorry. That must be hard on you.~
@86   = ~Do you really think I care about this, Will? You've found the wrong person to talk about such matters.~
@87   = ~Are you sure you don't want to ask? There's nothing wrong with knowing, and perhaps it'll give you some peace. They might have lived a good life.~
@88   = ~You're right. Dwelling in the past does no good for anyone. Just like the cities we discussed, the past is long gone. You're living a new life, in a new world.~
@89   = ~I don't want to discuss your pesonal matters, Will. Let us move on.~
@90   = ~It's fine. I'm just thinking aloud, nothing more and nothing less.~
@91   = ~I still think you should ask the spirits about your parents. What have you to lose?~
@92   = ~Just remember them as they were. Knowing what they have become might not be a good idea.~
@93   = ~If you need advice, go ask someone else. This is not my problem.~
@94   = ~I need to think more carefully about this. Maybe if I knew they were fine...~
@95   = ~Yes, I suppose you're right. They're long gone now, but... with my current state. I can't help but wonder if I belong in the past as much as they do.~
@96   = ~You have a great impact in the current time, Will. I think you live, just... in a different way.~
@97   = ~You've got an impact on the Realms, even as you are now. You're more than just an echo of the past, you're just as alive as me, or the people we meet.~
@98   = ~You might belong in the past, but it doesn't mean you're not important now either.~
@99   = ~You're just a waste of energy. Now may we move on?~
@100  = ~An impact? Hmm... I've never thought of it that way.~
@101  = ~It's good to know that you do not underestimate me.~
@102  = ~Anyways, don't misunderstand me. It's not that I think lowly of myself. After all, not everyone has the ability to speak with spirits. Not everyone had a chance to become a part of the Visionhive, and lastly... not everyone might get a second chance at existing. I'm well aware of that.~
@103  = ~I reckon you understand that our pasts are bound tightly with who we are now. So I won't give you any kind of bunk. After all... you are a child of Bhaal.~
@104  = ~I wasn't certain how much you knew of my heritage, Will. It seems you knew a lot after all.~
@105  = ~How did you know that? I never told you anything of my father or... or anything else!~
@106  = ~I know less than you think. To me, you're just <CHARNAME>, the one who shapes your own future. You alone choose what you do. Even if you might have potential no one else does, it's your decisions, your mind and soul that make you, not your blood.~
@107  = ~You entered the Visionhive while I was still there. We - shamans, that is - see more than most. Not to mention, I've heard the whispers and words of those we've met. Remember this, though: to me, you're just <CHARNAME>
You've been in Visionhive, when I was still in there. And we, shamans, see more. Not to mention the whispers and discussions of these we met. But remember: to me, you're <CHARNAME>, the one who shapes your own future. You alone choose what you do. Even if you might have potential no one else does, it's your decisions, your mind and soul that make you, not your blood.~
@108  = ~Bhaal may have been a cruel and vicious god, but he is dead, and cannot affect you and anything you do.~
@109  = ~Sometimes I feel like my decisions were made the day he sired me. Many things were set since then, such as my inability to have a peaceful life.~
@110  = ~Thank you. It's good to see someone else who actually believes I'm more than an evil entity waiting to devour the souls of the innocent, or what have you.~
@111  = ~On the contrary, I'm actually quite proud of my heritage.~
@112  = ~I see. Yes, that must be more than troublesome for you. But I hope you'll find the peace you desire one day regardless.~
@113  = ~Heh, no. As far as I know, children of Bhaal do not devour souls. Ghastlycleavers may do such a thing, but Bhaalspawns? No, not really.~
@114  = ~You are? Well... good for you, I suppose.~
@115  = ~I will bother you no longer, then.~
@116  = ~Were you told interesting stories when you were young? About magical places, peculiar beasts and breathtaking lands?~
@117  = ~My childhood wasn't that interesting, but the innkeeper of Candlekeep, Winthrop, told me a few stories. Why do you ask?~
@118  = ~Not that many. If it were stories I was after, I would sneak into the main library to wade through some old books. Usually I'd find a good tale or two.~
@119  = ~I'm not particularly interested in such nonsense. I prefer seeking action in real life over old fairy tales.~
@120  = ~I'm sorry, Will, but we have no time for small talk right now.~
@121  = ~So you must know some good tales, then! Perhaps we could exchange a few some time.~
@122  = ~Really? Heh, I find that hard to imagine. I always found tales to be inspiring in how... unusual... they were.~
@123  = ~I always found stories enchanting. As a kid, I often snuck away from my home - no matter the time of day - to seek out wandering storytellers at the local inns. Whenever I found one, I wouldn't leave until I hear all their best stories.~
@124  = ~You must have really loved doing that.~
@125  = ~Gods, you must have been a really annoying kid!~
@126  = ~We've all done something like that in our childhoods. I find that our rules and patterns change as we grow up.~
@127  = ~Sorry, but we should really get going.~
@128  = ~Well, I certainly did!~
@129  = ~Well, I suppose there are a few who would agree with you.~
@130  = ~I suppose you're right.~
@131  = ~Perhaps I've told you this before, but... because of my love for such tales, my mother called me "will-o-wisp". You know, using a play on my name with those mysterious beings. Those stories defined me. I thought perhaps things would be the same with you as well.~
@132  = ~Yes, I suppose it was similar. Not that it's an easy thing to say that I was defined by tales of adventurers, heroes and mysteries. It didn't seem all that serious at the time, but those things built me up to what I am now.~
@133  = ~I don't think it was. I always knew those stories were mere fiction. I think what defined me was the real experience, seeing the roads, cities, gold, people - all of it - with my own eyes.~
@134  = ~I really don't want to discuss it, Will. We should be going.~
@135  = ~You know, I'm quite happy to hear that. It's good to know that I wasn't the only one who felt that way.~
@136  = ~I guess we're all motivated by different things, right? Thank you for your honest answer, <CHARNAME>.~
@137  = ~Before we move on, may I ask you one more question?~
@138  = ~Sure. What is it?~
@139  = ~I'm sorry, but now's not the time.~
@140  = ~If you had the chance... would you change your past? If you could change any of your actions, or decisions, or even the words you have said and... those that you should have said.~
@141  = ~I think so. I've made my share of poor decisions, and there are words which I should've said, but didn't. If I could change them, I would.~
@142  = ~No. I may have made mistakes and said things I shouldn't have, but they're part of my past now. I wouldn't be the same without those things.~
@143  = ~I don't know. I don't think anyone could answer that without the actual chance to change things. Only then would we know for sure whether the cost would be worth it.~
@144  = ~I see. I think I'll need some time to think on it. Thank you for listening.~
@145  = ~I understand what you mean. You're a wise <PRO_MANWOMAN> to believe that. I think I'll need some time to think on what you've said.~
@146  = ~Perhaps you may be right about that. We may never know what else we could've done while bound to our current circumstances. I'll need some time to think on it.~
@147  = ~Anyways, I'm sorry if my question dampened your mood. That was never my intention. In truth, I value the opinions you are willing to share with me.~
@148  = ~We should get moving. There is still much more to see and do.~
@149  = ~Fine. I won't bother you anymore.~
@150  = ~Is it time for you to rest, <CHARNAME>? Shall I keep the fire burning?~
@151  = ~Sure, that would be helpful, thanks. What about you? Will you be reading or something while we rest?~
@152  = ~I think everyone's aware of their duties by now. I shouldn't need to repeat them. Good <DAYNIGHT>.~
@153  = ~No, not this time.~
@154  = ~I've been considering your words, and I've made up my mind. I will commune with the spirits to find out what happened to my parents. Although I'd rather not know the details, I want to be certain that they were happy.~
@155  = ~I understand. Will you begin now? Can I stay and do something?~
@156  = ~Whatever you intend to do, I want no part of it. I'm exhausted. Take care of it on your own.~
@157  = ~Yes, stay. You need not do anything, as I can do this on my own. Join me at the fire and I may begin.~
@158  = ~(He kneels by the fire, and a moment of silence passes before he begins to whisper a strange chant. His arms reach out and straighten as his fingertips touch the serpentine tongues of the flames. Will lowers one hand to trace symbols in the ashes while he touches the bones on his necklace with his other.)~
@159  = ~(Suddenly, he stops- and all is silent save for the sound of the wind brushing against the fire, launching sparks where the firewood is still fresh and wet. After several moments, the spectre finally turns to look at you.)~
@160  = ~They... were happy.~
@161  = ~My parents lived for almost two decades after my departure. Although they missed me, they never lost hope. They prayed to the gods - Tymora, Waukeen, even Lathander - not for me to return, but to... "light my road, and keep the darkness at bay". I... didn't care to hear more. It's enough to know they they lived a good life, even I was missed. I feel as though a massive burden was lifted from my heart.~
@162  = ~You still don't seem very happy, though.~
@163  = ~That's good. They were still happy. Everything was fine... *is* fine.~
@164  = ~Meh... I think I'll go to bed now. I thought it'd be more interesting than that...~
@165  = ~Did the spirits tell you all of that?~
@166  = ~It's... fine. This was the first time I've ever asked the spirits about anything personal. I didn't even know if they would answer my questions, but they did. It wasn't much, but... like I said, I didn't want to know more.~
@167  = ~Yes... once again, you're right. I'm glad you are, too.~
@168  = ~Yes. Though they didn't tell me much more... but it was all I cared to know.~
@169  = ~Would you join me by the fire for a while before you retire? I have a thought or two I'd like to share with you.~
@170  = ~Of course. What is it?~
@171  = ~No. I'm too tired. Find someone else to talk to.~
@172  = ~I've been considering your words, and I've decided you were right. I will not ask the spirits of my parents' fates. It was my decision to leave and I must live with the consequences of it. My life is my own responsibility, and even now... beyond life, I am still responsible for my own self. Knowing the past I did not choose would be akin to greed... greed for knowledge, control over the past.~
@173  = ~Perhaps. But it may also be a sign that are unable to accept the possible consequences of your actions.~
@174  = ~I don't feel like talking about this, Will. Your past is your own business, not mine. Find someone else to bother with your doubts.~
@175  = ~The power to commune with spirits is a valuable one. You can do better than knowing your family matters. The location of valuable power - magical artifacts and the like - for example... now, that would be impressive.~
@176  = ~Bah, I thought this would be about something important. If you've got nothing else to say, I'm off to bed.~
@177  = ~Hmm, you're a brutally honest person, <CHARNAME>. Though... your words may be true, even if only partially. My choice to keep the past secret from myself was a difficult one, but now... I feel it was the correct one.~
@178  = ~Spirits are not mere signposts that lead towards unliving treasure or power, <CHARNAME>. But I agree that the power to ask should be reserved for serious matters.~
@179  = ~(He gazes wistfully at the nearby fire for a while before continuing.)~
@180  = ~Gods, what I wouldn't give for the chance to share a drink with you right here, right now. It would be nice to remember that feeling of warmth once again!~
@181  = ~Heh, I know what you mean. That would be rather nice.~
@182  = ~I don't drink, Will. Though I can see why you'd miss the feeling.~
@183  = ~It's getting late, Will, and I'm looking to have some rest right now. Go and do... whatever it is you do while we sleep. Good <DAYNIGHT>.~
@184  = ~You know... I never told you the reason I left, did I? All I said was that I distanced myself from my family.~
@185  = ~You don't need to tell me anything you don't want to.~
@186  = ~I was going to ask eventually. Why did you leave? Just to see the world?~
@187  = ~Not interested. We're not close enough for me to care. I just want a chance to get some rest.~
@188  = ~It's fine. I've got nothing to be ashamed of.~
@189  = ~I... was attracted to someone. Kirian. He was the son of one of my father's business partners. But I didn't have the courage to tell anyone. Not my father, nor the target of my feelings.~
@190  = ~It wasn't because my father would oppose it. I know he wouldn't, and neither would my mother. I just... couldn't find the right words.~
@191  = ~Kirian and I spoke often of our contracts and everyday matters, and we shared an interest in art, but... we never said anything about emotional issues. If I had said anything, perhaps I would've gained the support I needed, but, well... I kept my distance up to the end... until I finally left.~
@192  = ~Perhaps your family sought an heir and you found that problematic?~
@193  = ~Why wouldn't you say anything to him? You had a father who would've supported you. Not everyone has such luck.~
@194  = ~You, shy of your own feelings? I would never have imagined it.~
@195  = ~This 'Kirian'... do you think he knew? Did you never show any signs? He might've even felt the same way.~
@196  = ~Ha! No, I doubt that was the problem. My parents weren't the type to insist upon things. They were reasonable folk - always grateful for any joys in their lives. They would argue once in a while, but who doesn't?~
@197  = ~I suppose it was because I was just a child. I lacked experience, and my interests were in reading and... collecting spiders in glass jars. I didn't know the first thing about talking of feelings or attractions.~
@198  = ~Really? Even as I am, I still consider myself rather shy! I suppose it's because you're always focused on what I am, or the fact that I can talk freely to the dead.~
@199  = ~No, I doubt it. Not that it matters anymore. I'm old enough to recognize my feelings for what they were - a childish crush, nothing more.~
@200  = ~Heh... it seems like I have gotten sentimental again. And there is more to tell - the first time I truly felt in love, for example.~
@201  = ~Ah, gods. I'd feel so much better talking about such things with warm ale in hand. Regardless... I think we've talked more than enough for one <DAYNIGHT>. You should get some rest.~
@202  = ~I see. I won't bother you anymore, then.~
@203  = ~May I have a moment, <CHARNAME>? I have something for you.~
@204  = ~Oh, is it a gift? I love gifts!~
@205  = ~You got something for me? Why?~
@206  = ~Not now, Will. We've got things to do.~
@207  = ~I hope you'll enjoy it as much as anything else you've recieved from a friend.~
@208  = ~Consider it my thanks. We've talked quite a lot, and I felt I should give you a token of my appreciation.~
@209  = ~Here. I mentioned my regret at being unable to share a drink with you when we last spoke, but I forgot that you, unlike me, can drink. I thought this ale could serve as an apology for only thinking of myself, when your state is far different from mine.~
@210  = ~I'm afraid, my friend, that you'll have to drink for the both of us, heh.~
@211  = ~Well, it looks like a nice brew, at least. Thank you.~
@212  = ~I'm sorry, Will, but I said I don't drink. I'm afraid you've wasted your gold on me.~
@213  = ~You really shouldn't have. But... still, thank you.~
@214  = ~Whatever. We've got work to do, so we'd best move on for now.~
@215  = ~I'm glad you like it. I... well, took it from a bar and left a few coins behind. I couldn't just walk up and buy it, after all. The living don't usually deal with customers like me.~
@216  = ~Right... I forgot. Still, I think you'd like to give it a try. After all, your life hasn't been easy, and no one's ever died from just one drink. It's up to you what you do with it. Give it to someone you care for if you don't want it.~
@217  = ~There was a time when I had forgotten the sound of my own voice... it was while I was still within the Visionhive. It was a peculiar thing to remember. With you, however...~
@218  = ~With you, everything is different. We talk, explore, and behold things both wonderful and terrible. Heh... sometimes, I even manage to forget that I am dead.~
@219  = ~What was it like living in the Visionhive?~
@220  = ~Right, I get it, life in the grotto was weird. Now can we drop it?~
@221  = ~Inside the grotto, I was just one of many. I felt safe, but it was always difficult to tell which thoughts were mine, and which belonged to others. I always knew how the others felt, and they knew how I felt. Everything was tangled, as if my actions where part of someone else's life.~
@222  = ~It's hard to explain without experiencing the feeling yourself.~
@223  = ~That sounds terrible. Living without any privacy, without any... individuality.~
@224  = ~It all sounds rather amazing to me.~
@225  = ~How many spirits gathered to create the Visionhive, exactly? There must be quite a few dozens of them.~
@226  = ~When you talk, all I hear is: "blah, blah, blah, spirits, blah, blah, visions, blah"! Shall we move on now, or must I continue to endure this nonsense?~
@227  = ~It's not as bad as you'd think. Privacy matters more when you're alive. When you've passed on, nothing is taboo. All are equal in their experiences. There is no shame in the knowledge.~
@228  = ~Yes, but it also means making sacrifices. You wouldn't feel anything the way you feel now. At the same time, you'd be guaranteed safety. It's a matter of deciding whether the price is worth it.~
@229  = ~More, much more. It's at least hundreds of dozens at this point in time.~
@230  = ~My existence here is nothing like the Visionhive. Here, I am a different shade of color altogether. Different to what I was before I died, and different to what I was inside the grotto. Perhaps that, too, is a godly power you possess - reshaping the very being of those that you meet.~
@231  = ~But this has little to do with you, my friend. Come, more adventures await us. And don't forget to enjoy that ale.~
@232  = ~I thought you would appreciate having a small break, but clearly I was wrong. So be it.~
@233  = ~I would like to ask you a question, <CHARNAME>, about your friend, the one taken from you... Imoen, right? I know little of her outside of what you have told me. Do you love her?~
@234  = ~Do I love her? Well, sort of like a sibling, yes. We grew up together.~
@235  = ~She's definitely important to me, but no, I can't say I love her.~
@236  = ~We're not lovers, if that's the impression you had. She's like my little, occasionally annoying sister.~
@237  = ~No, not really.~
@238  = ~I'm not going to discuss Imoen with you, Will. Leave me.~
@239  = ~Right, I understand. What about the mage... Irenicus, was it? How, exactly, did he capture you?~
@240  = ~It's a long story. He was there during the siege on Dragonspear Castle, haunting me. Then, once it was all over, tensions... rose. I was forced to flee for my life, only to be captured by his minions. Myself, Imoen, and my companions. My next memory was waking up in his dungeon. He performed... experiments on me. Well, it was more like torture, really.~
@241  = ~It wasn't a grand capture or anything. He... simply observed me for a long time, then sent a handful of men to capture me.~
@242  = ~That is none of your business, Will, and I'm not in the mood to indulge you. My past is not something I wish to divulge with you, understand?~
@243  = ~I see. I didn't know you had fallen into a trap, or that this man had followers. I still know very little of your own past.~
@244  = ~I only asked about Imoen because I wondered... wondered if your relationship was more than friendship. I was about to tell you more of my past, of my first time falling in love after I left home, after realizing my feelings for Kirian were nothing more than a fleeting crush.~
@245  = ~I'm interested in knowing. Start from the beginning. Who was this person?~
@246  = ~That's your own private business, Will. I think you've misunderstood the terms of our relationship. We are not here to be friends. Fall in line and let's move on.~
@247  = ~The story of you and your first love, eh? I'm all ears.~
@248  = ~His name was Higam, and he was a lieutenant. He was twenty-six when we first met, and I was two years his junior. At that time, I had already left my home for a while. While I travelled through the groves south of Trademeet, I discovered him, badly hurt and alone.~
@249  = ~His own people had abandoned him. He was poisoned, and they decided he wouldn't make it and wasn't worth carrying. They left him a knife to end his suffering. By the time I found him, he was only half-conscious, lying under a willow tree. Surrounding him were just some old bandages and a nearly empty bottle of whiskey.~
@250  = ~I brought him to shelter and treated him. He was drowning in sweat and pain, but he got better with time. After three days, he finally woke up, confused and afraid. But I managed to calm him down, and I brought supplies to our temporary home - water, herbs, some mushrooms and a few loaves of bread. Heh... we spent our days living on bread and soup, occasionally some berries when I found them. I even caught a fish once, and we considered it a great feast.~
@251  = ~After a week, his outer body had all but healed. The only damage left was in his heart. Still, if he lived carefully, he could still live a few happy years, perhaps as long as a decade, but...~
@252  = ~Heh, I remember how much we talked. He would always tell me war stories he was a part of. Sometimes I wondered if he made a few up to impress me!~
@253  = ~What happened next?~
@254  = ~Are you trying to bore me to death with this pitiful story?~
@255  = ~Well, we had a few bad moments, an argument or two, and we had a hard time understanding each other at times, but despite that, we grew fond of each other. We lived and ate together, watched over each other, and grew closer every day. We enjoyed every moment we spent together and I... I could honestly say that we were happy.~
@256  = ~It must have ended eventually, though. May I ask how he...~
@257  = ~You were both safe and in love. I'm sure both of you had good reason to feel happy.~
@258  = ~Bah, this tale is making me such to my stomach with its bittersweet taste. I'll hear no more of it.~
@259  = ~...died?~
@260  = ~Heh, well, I knew I was happy, at least. I only hope he felt the same. There was something about the way he looked at me. That's why I believed he loved me.~
@261  = ~Eventually, we finally decided to move out of our home. But we were careless, and stepped into a bear's territory, and we were attacked. When we tried to flee, the beast bit deeply into my shoulder and slashed my arm with its claws. Though we managed to escape it, I was losing a lot of blood. I could barely move, and I... I guess I fell.~
@262  = ~This time, it was Higam who took care of me. He hunted for food to keep me alive, cleaned my wounds, stayed awake on watch to make sure my blood didn't lure hungry predators. The nine years I lived since then were all thanks to him. But Higam...~
@263  = ~He grew weaker as a result. Almost every bit of food and water he managed to gather, he gave to me. I was too weak to protest, but I told him he was dying, that his state was too serious not to care for himself, but he only cared about me, rather than the fact that he nearly died those few months back. I couldn't save him a second time.~
@264  = ~I'm sorry, Will.~
@265  = ~That was a cruel ending to a sad tale, but... at least you were happy, if only for a while.~
@266  = ~Did you never find another that you could love as much?~
@267  = ~Bah, this is crap. Did you have a reason to feed me this rot?~
@268  = ~It's... alright. I came to terms with my loss a long time ago, even though it was hard... very damn hard.~
@269  = ~Yes... yes, I was. I know that. I still value the time we spent together, short as it was.~
@270  = ~Never.~
@271  = ~I wasn't exactly celibate since then. I still shared my bedroll with a few, but... my feelings were never the same with anyone else. My necklace... the strap belonged to Higam. It's not much, I know, but it was the only thing I could take. He owned nothing else. But it was still better than nothing.~
@272  = ~Facing a great loss is always difficult.~
@273  = ~I know. I felt the same way when I lost Gorion... the only father I knew.~
@274  = ~That is why I won't give up on Imoen. She's too dear to me. Even if what we share isn't love, I doubt I could live the same way if I lost her.~
@275  = ~Yes, it is.~
@276  = ~This is why I make an effort not to grow attached to others. It makes things easier.~
@277  = ~I don't think I can accept that so easily.~
@278  = ~Then you know the bitter taste of losing another you care for. It's... oddly relieving.~
@279  = ~Anyways, I think that's enough gloomy talk. We must have something we can do, right? I shouldn't slow you down. We can continue another time, my friend.~
@280  = ~You may have no choice, but there is still a chance. That's enough for now, we should move on, right?~
@281  = ~Yes... well, either way, I think we've talked enough about death, wouldn't you agree? We should move on, right?~
@282  = ~True, but isn't that in itself also a loss? I think I'll leave you with that thought. It's time for us to fall back in line and move on, right?~
@283  = ~I think it will be more difficult to deny it than you think. Perhaps you have yet to lose someone you truly care about.~
@284  = ~Come, we should move on. We must have something we can do, right?~
@285  = ~I see that I have picked the wrong time to talk to you. Fine, I won't bother you any longer.~
@286  = ~A copper for your thoughts, <CHARNAME>? You look as though you are lost in thought.~
@287  = ~Just thinking of Irenicus. As well as everything he's done to me.~
@288  = ~I'm thinking about Imoen. She could be anywhere, and in any condition by now.~
@289  = ~Oh, you must be mistaken. I was simply watching the embers.~
@290  = ~I was just thinking about tomorrow. Wondering what the next day will bring.~
@291  = ~It's none of your business.~
@292  = ~I see. I thought I should talk to you, as I don't want you to trouble yourself too greatly. Though we still have much to do, I believe your future will be bright... brighter than merely existing.~
@293  = ~I was wondering... what will you do once you've succeeded? Once Irenicus is stopped, and you are reunited with your friend?~
@294  = ~I haven't thought that far yet.~
@295  = ~I'd like to start a family. I want to be with someone I love, begin a peaceful life. Well, perhaps we'd start another adventure here and there, but it'll be by choice, rather than fate.~
@296  = ~I don't see myself anywhere else but in the adventurer's life. I want excitement, I want to find ancient ruins, lost civilizations, forgotten artifacts, trinkets that will allow me to do things beyond the ordinary.~
@297  = ~I want power. I want to be stronger, greater than anyone else. I don't want to be the test subject or pawn of anyone else ever again.~
@298  = ~Hmm... how about becoming a gourmet chef and building my own tavern? Serving guests, preparing mouth-watering feasts every evening? Yes, that would be the life of my dreams!~
@299  = ~That's none of your business, Will. Give me a break, will you?~
@300  = ~I suppose you still have all the time in the world. I doubt your journey will end in the next month, or the one after that.~
@301  = ~A family, huh? I suppose that is what most would want, to live with the man or woman of their dreams...~
@302  = ~You want fun and excitement, fame and riches, is that it? You have a thirst to find places forgotten by the world, filled with magic and secrets. I can see why you'd never grow bored.~
@303  = ~You seek power, then. I see Irenicus must have planted quite a strong seed within you.~
@304  = ~A tavern? Heh, quite an idea. I expected something grander, but now that you've said it... that might not be so bad.~
@305  = ~It's quite an important thing, you know, to have a plan. Not just for the near future, but the distant one as well. Our goals shape us, both body and spirit. No matter what it is we seek, we change... change our shape and harden our minds to reach it.~
@306  = ~I sense regret, Will. Is that what you're feeling?~
@307  = ~And what if someone lacks that goal? What do you think happens then?~
@308  = ~I'm not in the mood to delve into philosophical matters, Will.~
@309  = ~Yes. But I'm afraid everyone does, <CHARNAME>.~
@310  = ~Nothing, I think. Not a lot, and not a little, just... nothing.~
@311  = ~I've been thinking that perhaps even Irenicus may feel some regret. There may have been betrayal or unaccomplished goals in his past, things that still haunt him.~
@312  = ~It may be small yet still significant, or it may be so overpowering even someone with his power can't overcome. The possibilities are finite, and no matter what it may be... something must have happened to him.~
@313  = ~Are you trying to justify his actions?~
@314  = ~Do you believe that he may have been like us? That he did not start as cruel and vicious?~
@315  = ~Can we just end it here? I'm not in the mood to ponder things with you, Will.~
@316  = ~No, absolutely not. His actions are unforgivable. Still, I can't help but wonder, to try and understand... but not excuse, no.~
@317  = ~I believe nobody is born cruel and vicious. If that were the case, should you not have become the Lord of Murder long before now? No. Our actions shape us, and we then make our own goals.~
@318  = ~But this should be about you, not him. How are you feeling? I know a lot has happened and I fear only more will come.~
@319  = ~Fine, I guess. There's much to do, but I'm fine.~
@320  = ~I've been better, but... well, I hope something better will come soon.~
@321  = ~Not great. I'm beginning to wonder if there is any hope awaiting me.~
@322  = ~Stop reminding me, would you? Leave me be, I need some rest.~
@323  = ~Good, that's good. We'll stop this madman who has distorted your path.~
@324  = ~Rest now. Our journey will continue when you awaken, no sooner.~
@325  = ~Find hope, <CHARNAME>. Everything will become right once more, and if not, we'll make it.~
@326  = ~But rest now. Tomorrow will be a better day.~
@327  = ~Ah, I understand you'd rather remain alone. As you wish.~
@328  = ~Come and see the finest wares of Rattlemoth's Company! Ah, good day to you! Would you like to see our wares?~
@329  = ~Rattlemoth's Company? Might I ask the name of whom created this company, mister...?~
@330  = ~Boyerd Rattlemoth. Please, do not call me "mister", just Boyerd will do. I'm not my father.~
@331  = ~As for its creator, well... the company was founded generations ago, by... erm, I believe his name was Basstler Rattlemoth. Why do you ask? ...erm, are you feeling well, sir? You are looking awfully pale.~
@332  = ~Yes, I'm fine. I asked because... well, I value companies who are true to their roots. I'm glad you can still remember the one who started this business.~
@333  = ~I'm sorry, but I need to speak with my friend. Good day to you, Boyerd.~
@334  = ~Welcome to Rattlemoth's Company. Would you like to see our wares?~
@335  = ~Yes. Show me what you've got.~
@336  = ~No, thank you.~
@337  = ~So... my father must have had another son. The Rattlemoth name survived... I have a brother, and the company is still alive.~
@338  = ~That's right! Rattlemoth was your family name, was it not?~
@339  = ~You didn't know about that? I suppose you must not have been the best son.~
@340  = ~That's right.~
@341  = ~You may be right. I should have known...~
@342  = ~I never told you my father's name. It was Basstler - the founder of the Rattlemoth Company. The young man over there is of my family. We share... once shared the same blood.~
@343  = ~Now you know exactly what happened. Your father had another child, his company remains and is still successful.~
@344  = ~It changes nothing now, Will. You no longer possess your blood, and you are no longer human. You are a spectre of a man who left his home long ago.~
@345  = ~It seems your parents had another kid.~
@346  = ~I feel much better knowing that. I wondered if my actions might have doomed my parents, if the time came when they were in need but had no one to offer them aid, but I was wrong. It's good to know my fears and doubts were unfounded.~
@347  = ~They might've replaced you, but that doesn't mean your actions didn't hurt them.~
@348  = ~It looks like they were not alone after all. You had no cause for worry, Will.~
@349  = ~That's all very nice, but I think we should move on.~
@350  = ~You action may have still hurt them, Will. Do not jump to the optimistic conclusion just yet.~
@351  = ~I would much rather think that there is still much humanity in me, <CHARNAME>. My body may be dead, but my thoughts, doubts and goals still live. Differently, but still. Anyway, it's good to know the doubts were unfounded, at least. I'm satisfied knowing my parents were well after all.~
@352  = ~They might've replaced you, but that doesn't mean they didn't miss you.~
@353  = ~Do not jump to the optimistic conclusion just yet. You might have hurt them greatly.~
@354  = ~Of course that's true, but at least... at least they weren't alone. At least they lived long enough to raise another child to love.~
@355  = ~They might have not been alone, Will, but their son decided to leave them. I have a feeling that you think of the situation in quite a simple way. It's complicated and even thought they had another child, you might have hurt them.~
@356  = ~They might have loved the other kid, but that doesn't matter they forgot about you. Your doings might have had a great influence on their life. I think that leaving them could be a bit... egocentric of you.~
@357  = ~But maybe... Eh, nevermind. Forget I said something. They indeed seem to have a nice life.~
@358  = ~So you believe I made a mistake leaving them?~
@359  = ~Maybe. They would do everything to make you happy, but you decided to leave them.~
@360  = ~No. You did what you thought was best, but please, do not say they were fine because they had another child. That may be disrespecting their true feelings. We can't know how they felt.~
@361  = ~Whatever. Can we go now?~
@362  = ~Hmm. Well... I...~
@363  = ~You think so...? Well...~
@364  = ~Somewhere deep inside I know that this may be true. Yes, it was me who decided to leave. Yes, I focused on my own feeling. And finally yes - I might have wounded them greatly, in a way that may not be healed. But I do cared about them. About what we had. About their teachings.~
@365  = ~I may sound as if I did not care, but I did, <CHARNAME>. But all I can do now is believing they still had a reason to feel joy. I hope they other child made them proud. And that maybe there were times when they still thought of me fondly.~
@366  = ~Anyway, I would also like to thank you that we came here and met Boyerd. But we should be going now.~
@367  = ~*breathes* Yes. I feel as though a huge burden was just lifted from my shoulders.~
@368  = ~Thank you for bringing us here. I'm glad I had a chance to meet Boyerd... my blood. I won't tell him the truth, but... at least I find out. At least I know now.~
@369  = ~Are you sure? It might give you proper closure.~
@370  = ~Fine. Let's move on.~
@371  = ~Yes. Knowing that his grand, grand, grand... uncle is now a spectre won't do him any good. He's better off free of me. Come now, we should get going.~
@372  = ~Lead on, then.~
@373  = ~I see you've found someone you can be close to, <CHARNAME>. Perhaps even someone you can love? If that is the case, then I'm glad.~
@374  = ~I think I have, yes. Thank you for noticing.~
@375  = ~That's a bit too much. I might feel something, but love? That isn't a word I use lightly.~
@376  = ~This could go anywhere, but we'll see.~
@377  = ~My own affairs are no business of yours, Will. Don't bring this up again.~
@378  = ~It's good to know for sure.~
@379  = ~Well, that's understandable as well. The word does have great value.~
@380  = ~It always takes some time.~
@381  = ~I told you once about how I first fell in love, but...~
@382  = ~Heh, you never told me that you also like men. It seems we are more alike than I thought!~
@383  = ~Heh, you never told me that you like women. It makes me even happier knowing you've found someone to care for.~
@384  = ~Well, perhaps next time it will be you telling your ghostly brother stories of love and passion. (grin)~
@385  = ~Well, perhaps next time it will be you telling me stories about your chosen man!~
@386  = ~I won't give you a lecture on how magical or joyful a relationship can be. It'd only be the ramblings of a dead man. Such things are different for everyone, after all. You'll know whether you've found the right person eventually.~
@387  = ~Thank you. I hate it when people tell me how I should feel. It's good to finally hear someone saying something different.~
@388  = ~My goal was never to find 'true love' or anything like that. If this relationship isn't what I'm after, I'll end it if I must.~
@389  = ~I'm really excited about all of this, you know. I just hope I'm not the only one feeling this way.~
@390  = ~I don't want to discuss this any longer.~
@391  = ~Heh, why should anyone tell you how you should feel? If anyone does, ignore them. Your feelings are your own to command.~
@392  = ~Of course. You alone have the right to decide what is truly right for you.~
@393  = ~If you don't know yet, you'll probably find out soon.~
@394  = ~I hope you don't mind if I ask, but... was this your first...?~
@395  = ~No, it's not.~
@396  = ~Yes, but keep it between us. It's embarrassing, but I needed to find someone I really liked. I hope you understand.~
@397  = ~I'm not telling you that. That's my own business!~
@398  = ~I see. (grin) That's good. It's a healthy thing to be seeking bonds with others.~
@399  = ~I see! Well, I hope you'll enjoy the new experience!~
@400  = ~Well, I just hope it doesn't get too... *ahem* messy. It does happen sometimes... and it's never a good thing is you're not close to a body of water, or a full waterskin.~
@401  = ~...um, I should apologize for saying that. I usually don't talk about it. I suppose I shouldn't have said that out loud.~
@402  = ~Now you have me interested. Got any insight about that?~
@403  = ~Erm... I guess it's fine. Let's just move on.~
@404  = ~Trust me, I know how... sticky... things can get.~
@405  = ~Well, this talk suddenly went somewhere awkward. Let's forget either of us said anything.~
@406  = ~I don't want to talk about this stuff, Will.~
@407  = ~I'd rather not... let's just say that someone got overexcited and... things got a little awkward. It didn't stop us from laughing about it later, but I *really* would rather avoid getting into the details, heh. Let's just move away from this topic.~
@408  = ~Right...~
@409  = ~Huh. Well, I guess you do know how awkward it can get... erm, anyways, perhaps we should move on...?~
@410  = ~If that's what you want. Lead on, I'm right behind you.~
@411  = ~Ah... there are so many spirits here. So many echoes... screaming and whirling amidst the darkness...~
@412  = ~Is something alright, Will? You're acting rather strange ever since we entered.~
@413  = ~What are you talking about?~
@414  = ~I don't hear anything...~
@415  = ~We don't have time for this. Let's move.~
@416  = ~While we were still above the ground, all I heard were whispers, but here... the echoes are resounding all over the walls. I hear whispers of the past, present and future. Evewrything is weaving and curling, as though it were a pond willed with eels and snakes.~
@417  = ~Focus, Will.~
@418  = ~Just don't think about it. Distract yourself as best you can.~
@419  = ~Yes...~
@420  = ~Ah... I think I do feel a little better. This place is nothing like the Visionhive. Quite the opposite, actually. It is dead, filled with negative energy. I was overpowered earlier, but now I've recovered a bit.~
@421  = ~That's good. Do you know what we might find in this tomb?~
@422  = ~I see. Well, we should move on now.~
@423  = ~Traps, cold stones, shadows, carrion. Perhaps undead. Nothing that the living would consider pleasant, I fear.~
@424  = ~This place is an enclave for the dead. The living were never meant to come here, not for extended periods. Let's do what we must quickly, <CHARNAME>, so that we may leave as soon as possible.~
@425  = ~Fine. I'll do my best to ignore these strange whispers. Let's do what we must so we can leave this place as soon as possible.~
@426  = ~I was wondering, <CHARNAME>... do you feel happy as you are?~
@427  = ~That's difficult to answer. I don't know, really. Too much has happened in the time I left Candlekeep, far more than I ever expected to handle.~
@428  = ~I think I am. Even if life's kicked me in the rear a few times, it could've been much worse. I'm still alive, and I'm happy for that.~
@429  = ~I'm not, Will. So many people I cared for have fallen. First Gorion, then Khalid and Dynaheir. I never even had the chance to properly mourn them.~
@430  = ~Stop asking me these pointless questions, Will. Let's move on.~
@431  = ~This time must have been hard on you. No wonder you find it difficult to even know whether you're happy or not. Believe it or not, I find it saddening.~
@432  = ~I'm glad to hear that. I know terrible things have happened to you, first with your losses, then Imoen being taken from you, but you're a strong <PRO_MANWOMAN> to find happiness despite that.~
@433  = ~I'm really sorry to hear that. You should've at least had time to say your farewells.~
@434  = ~There were times for me as well where I felt weak and helpless. It was when I lost Higam, the one I loved. I was both sad and furious. I would drink until I drowned in ale, and I would stay silent for days. I stopped caring for anyone else, even if they called to me, I ignored them.~
@435  = ~But you recovered somehow.~
@436  = ~Wasn't that unfair to those people who needed you?~
@437  = ~Yes, I did. But it took time... a lot of time.~
@438  = ~Perhaps, but I considered losing Higam unfair as well. "Why should I save anyone, when I couldn't even save the one I loved most, or even myself?" I told myself that many times.~
@439  = ~I mean to say, <CHARNAME>... if you need any help... if you ever feel overwhelmed... let me know. I won't tell you everything will be alright, or nothing happened. I wouldn't lie to you. But I will listen. If you won't talk, we could sit and watch the fire burn. Anything that comforts you.~
@440  = ~Why are you being so kind?~
@441  = ~I don't need anyone, Will. I'm no weakling.~
@442  = ~Thank you. I'll keep that in mind.~
@443  = ~Because I can. You've helped me, and helped others even when they have nothing to give in return. You deserve this much.~
@444  = ~I am at your service, leader... friend.~
@445  = ~Heh... if I were alive, I would suggest having a pint, or a feast, but we both know the problems with that. I cannot drink or eat. Heh, I couldn't even smoke if I wished to. Such a pity.~
@446  = ~We can at least talk. That's enough for me.~
@447  = ~Did you smoke while you were alive?~
@448  = ~Whatever. Can we finally move on?~
@449  = ~I'm afraid that's all I can offer you. It's at least better than nothing.~
@450  = ~Once in a while, I might've burned a pipe of tobacco. I wouldn't call myself a smoker, but I can't pretend I was clean of it. That's all I had, though - I've tried Haunspeir and Redflower Leaves once or twice, but never more than that. Those aren't for me.~
@451  = ~Anyways, I feel we should move on. But if you need me, I'm always ready to listen.~
@452  = ~Fine. I won't bother you again.~
@453  = ~I need to confess something, <CHARNAME>. After I realized that you found someone close to you, I was reminded of myself... and how I felt when I met Higam. We might be separated now, but... seeing you find someone to bond with felt as though it has restored me.~
@454  = ~It certainly feels restorative to have someone who cares.~
@455  = ~Will, you realize this may not last forever, right? Don't get so attached. If I've learned anything, it's that anything - even bonds - may change.~
@456  = ~This is my life, Will, not yours. Please keep your distance, away from my business.~
@457  = ~These are my private matters, Will. I don't want you to get involved.~
@458  = ~Don't worry. I know that.~
@459  = ~What? Did you think I wanted to live your life? I was just expressing how glad I was to see my friend happy. If that bothers you...~
@460  = ~I'm sorry. I'm grateful that you'd feel that way. I just didn't want to feel pressured.~
@461  = ~Right, but... what if this doesn't work? What if something happens and we fall apart, and become merely companions again?~
@462  = ~I don't care. Just keep your distance.~
@463  = ~Heh, you're probably right. I'm sorry, it's just been a while since I've felt anything like how you're feeling now.~
@464  = ~There was something else I wanted to say, <CHARNAME>.~
@465  = ~I understand. No harm done.~
@466  = ~Look, I don't want you to think that I'm observing, or pressuring, or even judging you. The truth is that it's been too long since I've talked with the living. Ever since I became something more than a being of visions or dreams, I think I've choked slightly on it.~
@467  = ~I just want you to knwo that I... I consider you a true friend. A <PRO_BROTHERSISTER>. Not by blood, perhaps, but by bond.~
@468  = ~Lucky you. If we really shared blood, that'd make you a Bhaalspawn too! ...Heh, thank you, Will. I consider you a good friend, and I'm honored to have you.~
@469  = ~Look, Will, I just consider you a valuable companion. You're a shaman with useful skills and I could use them, that's all. This may disappoint you, but I'm not gonig to tell you any white lies.~
@470  = ~That's funny, because I also think of you like a brother, Will. A true one, one I can be proud of, not just another that shares my taint.~
@471  = ~Don't make me laugh, ghost. If you need sentiment, do your voodoo magic and call some spirits to entertain yourself. I'm not interested.~
@472  = ~Thank you.~
@473  = ~...Heh. I think this is starting to get a little mawkish for my tastes. We've said what we wanted to. Perhaps we should return to our tasks, then?~
@474  = ~You're right. Let's move on.~
@475  = ~There's something more I'd like to say to you.~
@476  = ~Yes? What is it?~
@477  = ~Do you really think we'll succeed? That we'll defeat Irenicus and any fiend he commands?~
@478  = ~Are you not afraid of me at all? You know the Bhaalspawn for what they are, as well as the evil of Bhaal. You must have known, even while you were alive.~
@479  = ~I can hardly admit it, but... I think I might be falling in love with you.~
@480  = ~Nothing. It's nothing. We should move on.~
@481  = ~I understand, <CHARNAME>. Thank you for telling me the truth. I suppose I've stolen enough of your time by now, so... lead the way.~
@482  = ~Come on, then.~
@483  = ~Yes. I believe we will. No matter how devious or powerful he may be, we are far from ordinary ourselves. We face him for a purpose, and we have a goal to strive for.~
@484  = ~I think Irenicus made a huge mistake the day he chose to cross the Bhaalspawn in front of me.~
@485  = ~No, I am not. Firstly, I do my best not to judge people before knowing them. Even if I did, I do not base my judgments on what others tell me, <CHARNAME>.~
@486  = ~Secondly - what have I to fear? Could you send me to the Nine Hells if you wished? Heh. In truth - I believed I could trust you. I think it was the best decision I could have made.~
@487  = ~You're... in love with me? I'm sorry, <CHARNAME>, but I considered you a <PRO_BROTHERSISTER>, not--I'm sorry. If I knew you felt that way, perhaps I should've make my thoughts more clear.~
@488  = ~You are a wonderful person and... doubtlessly a great lover, but... I am a dead man. You are not. I do not wander the Prime Material Plane in search of love.~
@489  = ~I'm sorry.~
@490  = ~I suppose I've misunderstood our relationship. I shouldn't have bothered you.~
@491  = ~A question for you, <CHARNAME>.~
@492  = ~What sort of women do you prefer, hmm? Heh. I know it isn't always the same as the one we choose, but there must be something that you feel drawn to.~
@493  = ~You ghostly bastard! Heh... actually, I like both men and women. It all depends on the specific person.~
@494  = ~What I like, hmm... I find uniqueness attractive. Something... special. Something that separates her from others.~
@495  = ~I find a clever mind attractive. Perhaps that is why I tend to fall for bookworms, heh.~
@496  = ~I'm a simple <PRO_MANWOMAN>. I fall for attractive women. That's just the way I am, ha!~
@497  = ~I like a woman who knows how to kick arse and take care of their own. I don't mind being rescued once in a while!~
@498  = ~I don't want to discuss it. Really.~
@499  = ~I see. I don't have much experience there, so it would take me a while to see some kind of pattern... if there is any at all!~
@500  = ~Hmm, I see... (He smiles playfully)~
@501  = ~What sort of men do you prefer, hmm? Heh. I was wondering if we possibly had similar tastes, or if you looked at... different characteristics.~
@502  = ~You little...! Heh... actually, I like both men and women, so I'd be surprised if you found any similar patterns.~
@503  = ~What I like, hmm... I find uniqueness attractive. Something different. Something that separates him from others.~
@504  = ~You know, I think I have a fetish for bearded me. Especially scratchy ones. Call me a freak if you will, but I fall head over heels for strong "beardomancers!"~
@505  = ~I like men who think with their minds. I can see myself with my ideal partner on a peaceful day, a book in one hand, a glass of wine in the other.~
@506  = ~I like a man I can protect, one that can depend on me. I enjoy helping those that I care for.~
@507  = ~I'm a simple <PRO_MANWOMAN>. I fall for strong, good-looking men.~
@508  = ~Sorry, but that's not something I'd discuss with you, Will!~
@509  = ~I see. Huh, I'm not really experienced there, and I won't pretend to be. You might be right in that I couldn't find anything similar.~
@510  = ~Hmm, I can imagine that. (He smiles playfully)~
@511  = ~"Beardomancer"? Hah! That's a good one. Speaking of beards... heh. You see my own, don't you? Why do you think I was drawn to Higam to begin with? Well, it was more than just that, but he was very- heh, I think you get the idea.~
@512  = ~The reason I asked was because I was wondering... have you ever felt ashamed of your affections?~
@513  = ~Gods, no! Why would you ask?~
@514  = ~I've never felt that, no. Remember, I wasn't raised by a complete family. Besides Gorion, there was only Imoen, who'd never judge me for anything. Although if I told Gorion I had feelings for, say, a Zhent, I can't say I wouldn't feel a bit of shame for that.~
@515  = ~I was confused by my own feelings at the beginning, but I'm not ashamed of it now. I'm happy with who I am.~
@516  = ~I was confused by my own feelings at the beginning... and even now, a little. It's always difficult to talk to others when you can never tell if they like you.~
@517  = ~I have, once...~
@518  = ~I don't want to talk about it. Let's move on.~
@519  = ~When I first fell for Kirian, I felt a bit ashamed of myself. Not anymore, of course, now that I know it was fine, but I still wouldn't know what to tell my father.~
@520  = ~Well, that would be quite a complicated situation indeed!~
@521  = ~Right. I understand.~
@522  = ~There's nothing to be confused about, <CHARNAME>. You are perfectly fine as you are.~
@523  = ~I see. I won't ask any further.~
@524  = ~I asked because I often wonder... why are so many people so ashamed of how they feel for others, whether those are men or women? Shouldn't we be free to decide how we look at others?~
@525  = ~So many are unwilling to talk about their feelings, as though they feel shame in their lives, their love or- or digity.~
@526  = ~There's no reason to feel shame. But it also takes bravery to admit that.~
@527  = ~People fear breaking the status quo. It's not always a matter of shame.~
@528  = ~I don't know, and honestly, I don't want to think about it. Can we leave this behind us?~
@529  = ~I think one must learn to accept themselves first. Perhaps shame comes when one isn't ready to do that.~
@530  = ~It's a hard question to answer, really... as much as I want to, I don't know what to tell you.~
@531  = ~I suppose you're right about that.~
@532  = ~The status quo? Why should that bother anyone? Must the majority's thoughts always be the way of things? People are diverse, each one has their own thoughts and feelings. Why should one's views be less valid than a hundred's?~
@533  = ~Perhaps you're right. I suppose that is why people create such personas.~
@534  = ~That makes two of us.~
@535  = ~I've been pondering this because I really wish it were easier. No matter how much time passes, some rules never seem to change.~
@536  = ~Would you be happy if your foster father - Gorion - had a chance to meet your chosen one?~
@537  = ~Yes. I wish that were possible.~
@538  = ~No, not really. I think it would be a bit awkward. We weren't that close anyway.~
@539  = ~I don't know... maybe?~
@540  = ~Mm. I... I would like my father to see Higam and I together, but that will never happen.~
@541  = ~But enough of all this, <CHARNAME>! There is more to do, more to see, right? Come, friend, our future awaits us!~
@542  = ~I suppose I shouldn't have bothered you.~
@543  = ~You're not too tired yet, are you, <CHARNAME>? What say you to a game of cards before you sleep?~
@544  = ~A game of chance, huh? Can I trust you not to ask spirits about my hand?~
@545  = ~Sounds like fun. Deal the cards.~
@546  = ~Nah, I'd rather just get some rest. See you in the morning.~
@547  = ~Huh, that actually didn't cross my mind. Not a bad idea.~
@548  = ~I promise I won't cheat by asking spirits about your hand. I'd rather save my powers for important questions.~
@549  = ~Fine, then. Let's play.~
@550  = ~I'd rather get some rest. See you in the morning, Will.~
@551  = ~Right, just let me shuffle the deck before I deal your cards... alright, now it's my turn... you have five, right? Alright, you may start.~
@552  = ~May I ask you something while we play? The last time we were in a city, I heard a rumor of the Bhaalspawn being fourteen-foot tall titans, smelling of sulphur and crushing anything in the way beneath their heels. What do you think about that?~
@553  = ~I wish I could do that! Maybe I'm not really a Bhaalspawn after all?~
@554  = ~People say strange things sometimes.~
@555  = ~Well, don't tell anyone, but... if I really wanted to, I could do that and more.~
@556  = ~Hah... maybe you aren't. Would that comfort you?~
@557  = ~Oh yes, they definitely do. Heh.~
@558  = ~Don't get me wrong, <CHARNAME>. I don't doubt your power for a second.~
@559  = ~I wonder how many more tales we'll hear of you before we're done.~
@560  = ~Anyways... it's your turn, <CHARNAME>. Let's be done before the fire burns out!~
@561  = ~Fine. Sweet dreams.~
@562  = ~Heh... you seem to be completely wasted, <CHARNAME>.~
@563  = ~Y-yesh! *hic* I- I am!~
@564  = ~Noooo, I'm not. I'm jusht... *hic* very, VERY happy! Look at that mug...! Whoa, that'sh not a mug...?~
@565  = ~Ugh... it'sh just... a l-lousy day. I needed a... *hic* drink, y'know.~
@566  = ~M-mind yer own bushinesh! *hic*~
@567  = ~Well, you're still sober enough to talk, I guess. How about walking? Can you stand? Gods, I don't think I've ever seen you this drunk! How much did you down, <PRO_BROTHERSISTER>?~
@568  = ~Jusht... *hic* a li'l... I think.~
@569  = ~Hnn... I jusht... kept chugging 'em as they came... up 'til that no-good bartender... shtopped me. *hic* Ruined my fun, that.~
@570  = ~M-mind your own businesh. Get outta my way!~
@571  = ~In that case... I think I've got another bottle down here somewhere...~
@572  = ~G-give it 'ere!~
@573  = ~I c-could just kiss you! Here, fill 'er up!~
@574  = ~N-nah, I've had enough... still gotta... long journey ahead...~
@575  = ~W-whatever. Just get outta my way, would ya?~
@576  = ~Ha! Do you really think I'd give you any more? No, no, no, definitely not. Another drop and you'd be as pale as I am.~
@577  = ~Good to see you've still got some sense in that head of yours! Heh.~
@578  = ~Haha... were you trying to show off your tough balls, or something? I'm sure they're large and impressive, but you really didn't need to empty all these bottles to prove it.~
@579  = ~Haha... were you trying to show off how tough you are? I see enough of that in battle, so there's no need for you to test yourself like this.~
@580  = ~Anyways, that's enough teasing from me. Do you need a hand?~
@581  = ~No, it... it's fine. Some fresh air would be good though.~
@582  = ~Hmm, yes... I- I could definitely use one.~
@583  = ~Nah, I'd be happy with a warm bed... or a roll... or anything warm and flat on the ground right about now...~
@584  = ~Right, lead on then. I'll be right behind you... (just in case you fall over and break your head...)~
@585  = ~Fine. I'm actually glad I have no ability to smell. I can imagine you'd need a warm bath when the day comes.~
@586  = ~Warm and flat on the ground, eh? I'm sure we can get that easily enough, heh. Come on, let's find you a nice place to lie down.~
@587  = ~I've been thinking about what you said to me the last time we talked.~
@588  = ~If you think we should talk about it, then I agree.~
@589  = ~Is it too much to ask if you've changed your mind?~
@590  = ~Must we bring this up again? We've shared our thoughts and feelings, and I'd rather continue than to chase after something that doesn't exist.~
@591  = ~Yes, I do think we should talk.~
@592  = ~I... I don't know.~
@593  = ~I'm not going to lie, you caught me off guard when you said those words. But... I just don't feel the same way.~
@594  = ~While I may appear like a normal ma, I'm... not. Not any more. This shape, this face that I wear is of someone long gone. I am not like you.~
@595  = ~This shape, and this face that I wear is that of a man long gone from this world. I cannot be like you. While I may have doubts like a living man, I cannot feel the same way. My presence to this world is tied by different bonds to yours.~
@596  = ~Does that mean you can't return my feelings?~
@597  = ~I understand. It's just that you're so normal in other ways that I forget about what you are.~
@598  = ~Look, I don't want to talk about this. I think you made yourself clear enough the last time we spoke.~
@599  = ~No. I can feel, but... differently to you. Even the feeling of standing here in front of you is entirely different to how you must feel.~
@600  = ~The fact that you understand somehow... doesn't make it any easier.~
@601  = ~I think we can both agree that this situation is... hard for the both of us.~
@602  = ~Will... look. Whatever I might have said to disturb you, I never meant to change the relationship we already had. Above all else, you are my friend. You have a right to feel however you may towards me, and I understand that. I'd rather we continue as honest friends than continue avoiding each other.~
@603  = ~No, it's not... not for me, at least. You've made your thoughts clear enough to me. For now, let's focus on what matters the most - our enemies and the task we must accomplish. We've already lost something that words will never bring back. Let's just forget about it and move on.~
@604  = ~You're probably right. You were just being honest with your words. I was confused... I still am, but that will pass. I should be glad you didn't keep it inside and slowly drown in your feelings while alone.~
@605  = ~I agree with you. We should try our best to work through this experience. It shouldn't stop us from talking with each other.~
@606  = ~Good. That settles it then.~
@607  = ~You know, on the other hand... I'm not so sure I'll be able to talk to you like I used after all of this. No, I changed my mind. We should keep our relationship strictly as allies. I can't just turn around and go back to being normal friends. I'm sorry I brought this up.~
@608  = ~That's good. We should move on for now, but I promise we'll have a chance to talk again soon.~
@609  = ~I see... so the situation is even clear to me now. If that's how you want it, then... let's just move on.~
@610  = ~<CHARNAME>, I felt I needed to ask if... if you're feeling alright? I thought a bit more about what you said. About the crush on me. You said you're fine and that we should keep working together, too, but I- I wanted to be sure that you're fine.~
@611  = ~It hurts to be rejected, but I'm fine now. At least you were honest.~
@612  = ~If you really cared, then you should've said something I liked. Just stay out of my way.~
@613  = ~No, it's fine. I should apologize for springing that on you. I understand your position and... I'm happy enough to be friends.~
@614  = ~I thought it was better than telling you a lie or avoiding you forever. I mean no offense, but... I wouldn't change my mind. Not then, and not now.~
@615  = ~Don't apologize. You're not at fault for admitting your feelings.~
@616  = ~I thought I should ask... just in case. I wonder if my presence is making you uncomfortable. If you want me to leave, then...~
@617  = ~No, don't. I'm really fine now.~
@618  = ~I- yes. I think that would be better. I'm sorry.~
@619  = ~You've got that much sense, at least. Get away from me.~
@620  = ~Don't even think about it. I want you to stay, and not because of my brief infatuation. That's behind me now.~
@621  = ~Good... that's good. I'm glad to know it.~
@622  = ~If that's all, I suppose now's a good time to move on. Come, friend! There is still much to do.~
@623  = ~I... I understand. Regardless of this choice, it has been an honor to travel with you. Fair winds to you, no matter what your future may be.~
@624  = ~Heh, fair enough.~
@625  = ~I'm sorry for bothering you.~
@626  = ~So you've decided to become a hero now? I'm not sure if that's a good idea.~
@627  = ~Why not? I thought you'd be happy that we're helping others.~
@628  = ~I'm not doing this to please you, Will. Just don't deter me from doing what I decide to.~
@629  = ~I'm not against it, but... all heroes must lose something. Can you affort losing more than you already have? I know you do this because you care for others, and I think it's noble, but you're risking your own life for it. Will you sacrifice everything you are for others?~
@630  = ~Maybe <PRO_HESHE> shouldn't sacrifice <PRO_HIMHER>self, but we can't just stand by when we have the power to help others either, Will. I thought you'd understand that, at least.~
@631  = ~I do understand, Nalia. I don't mind helping others, but I don't want to see <CHARNAME> fall for someone else's sake while <PRO_HISHER> own goals are unaccomplished.~
@632  = ~I haven't forgotten about myself, Will. I always save enough to take care of my own needs.~
@633  = ~Don't worry, Nalia. I agree with you. I want to make the world a bettter place both for others and myself. That's why I do all these things.~
@634  = ~Helping others is also my goal, Will. I refuse to stand by and watch the vile and repugnant harm the innocent. I want the world to be the best I can make it.~
@635  = ~These's benefit to me in these actions. There's rewards to be had in heroism. I don't care whether they call me a hero or a mercenary, so long as I get what I deserve for my actions.~
@636  = ~Whatever, Will, I'm not here to cater to your wishes. Let's just move on.~
@637  = ~That's good. I'd hate to see you lose your own path while helping others along their own.~
@638  = ~You're pretty confident that you'll be able to do that.~
@639  = ~I see.~
@640  = ~You must know the stories about all the greatest heroes. They are praised by the common folk, but all of them will lose something for their actions. It may be their family, their lives, their love or even their peace. It's a high price to pay.~
@641  = ~I can't tell you to ignore the plight of others, but you should remember that you are also suffering. You shouldn't sacrifice your own life for everyone else. Help if you must, but not at your own cost.~
@642  = ~Why are you telling me all of this now?~
@643  = ~I know what you're trying to say, Will. Don't worry. I know where to draw the line.~
@644  = ~I think I know the consequences of my actions better than you, Will.~
@645  = ~*sigh* Can we just drop it? We clearly aren't going to see eye to eye.~
@646  = ~Because people know of you now, and they all speak of you. They know to ask you to help them with their own problems, so that you'll save them from their troubles.~
@647  = ~If that is true, then I'm glad.~
@648  = ~I'll say this again. I'm not suggesting that you ignore the people who suffer and have their lives at stake. But does every man who lost their dog or their purse need our attention while Irenicus is ahead of you? I think you'd understand that.~
@649  = ~I didn't think you'd be too busy to even spare a minute to listen. Fine, then. Lead on.~
@650  = ~I- I can sense a strange presence here. There is a powerful force that is gripping onto me and- and is not letting go. These whispers, they... <CHARNAME>, what is happening?!~
@651  = ~This place...~
@652  = ~I think I understand now. This place... is a haven for spirits, and because of that, it beckoned me. It is like the Visionhive, yet... vile and cruel. Dark entities call this place home, <CHARNAME>. They scream out for blood, out of hunger, the urge to feed...~
@653  = ~Feed... on what?~
@654  = ~Are you about to say what I think you're going to say?~
@655  = ~...on us. Yes, I fear they desire to feed on us. Not only on our blood, but our energy, our dreams, and our hope. Everything that gives us life.~
@656  = ~Brilliant. Just brilliant! I don't suppose you know how to escape before we become lunch?~
@657  = ~Hmm... but there must be a way out, right?~
@658  = ~Hah! Sounds like there's some good fun waiting ahead of us.~
@659  = ~Hmm... I need to observe and think...~
@660  = ~Places like this must have some sort of protector or guardian. If we are to escape, we will have to deal with them... aggressively, if we must. That should weaken the veil that envelops this area.~
@661  = ~But wouldn't such a being be quite powerful?~
@662  = ~Alright. Let's look around. I've got better things to do than to wander around here aimlessly forever.~
@663  = ~No doubt. But we'll only know for sure by finding them. Quickly, before they find us first.~
@664  = ~You're right. I'm right behind you.~
@665  = ~*New things have entered my abode. Much different to the spiders and black elves that dwell in the Great Cave! I sense you, fleshling, from your breaths and energy to your inner urges. It was only the spirit at first, but I knew something more, something greater walked beside it.*~
@666  = ~So this creature sensed me first, did it? But... I think it knows who you are, <CHARNAME>.~
@667  = ~*Yes... I know of you, and what you are destined to become. Great potential sleeps within you, fleshling. The very word itself is almost engraved upon your essense. If I were to devour you, my power would no doubt increase tenfold. I would have the power to make my home greater, powerful beyond comprehension!*~
@668  = ~What?! You want to eat me?~
@669  = ~Oh, great...~
@670  = ~*Yes, fleshling. Was I not clear enough?*~
@671  = ~*I know you are not unfamiliar with places such as this, fleshling. I can read the word "Visionhive" within your mind. I can see the images of that pitiful grotto. It is but a speck compared to my dominion! This nest is destined to become great... it is the home of perennial energy.*~
@672  = ~*And you, fleshling... *you* are the key to its release.*~
@673  = ~I have no interest in your plans! Let us leave, lest you regret it.~
@674  = ~You want a fight, beast? Then that's what you'll get!~
@675  = ~*Your pitiful self serves only one purpose... to feed us, strengthen us.*~
@676  = ~That... that creature was the most spectacular thing I have seen in my life... as well as my afterlife. It was deadly as well. The energy it possessed was undoubtedly great. It's a pity it was wasted on instilling terror.~
@677  = ~Without it, this place will die, slowly but inevitably. I doubt a new protector will rise to take the role. But perhaps that is a good thing... the presence of this beast has corrupted the spirits that originally called this place home.~
@678  = ~You have seen the wisps. They were wild, cruel, more so than others of their kind. They yearned to feed on our energy.~
@679  = ~This place deserves to die. Hopefully it will be reborn as something better one day.~
@680  = ~Will, this is not the time to be discussing the fate of the monster nor that of its home. We need to get out of here as soon as possible.~
@681  = ~I hope so. We should check the beast's remains. Perhaps there is something that might aid us in our escape.~
@682  = ~Yes, you're right. We should check the beast's remains. Perhaps there is something that might aid us in our escape.~
@683  = ~Ah... we have arrived at the main cave. We can return to our original task, <CHARNAME>. Lead on.~
@684  = ~How are you feeling, <CHARNAME>? That change that was forced upon you was far too crual. I'm sorry.~
@685  = ~Why are you sorry?~
@686  = ~I doubt there was anything you could have done, Will. Please, don't pretend otherwise.~
@687  = ~Do you have a point, or are you just looking at me like a sick pet? I have no desired to be pitied. Give me a break so that we may move on.~
@688  = ~I just wish there was anything I could do. If only I was stronger, so that I may stop that scum, Irenicus, from doing anything else.~
@689  = ~You seem irritated, <CHARNAME>. I only meant to say that I care.~
@690  = ~I am growing worried about your current state, <CHARNAME>. I don't know what Irenicus did to you, but you seem... incomplete. As if something inside you is now gone. It's as if-~
@691  = ~It's as if I lost my soul? Yes, that's what happened. Don't worry, though. We'll get it back.~
@692  = ~I appreciate your support, Will. If I sounded bother by your concern, I apologize. I just... feel weakened, as well as unwhole.~
@693  = ~I could tolerate your inane prodding for a while, but I've had enough. Get out of my way!~
@694  = ~Will... why? Why must this all happen to me? Why, in all the Nine Hells, must there always be after my life, or my soul or... just my undoing? I'm tired... so tired.~
@695  = ~We will. I swear to you, we will. We'll find Irenicus, and do whatever it takes to make sure you're restored.~
@696  = ~I can sense it. Apology accepted, <CHARNAME>... I understand.~
@697  = ~I don't know. I'm sorry. Perhaps it is all because of your blood, but, believe me - things will change for the better if we force it to. That's what we'll do.~
@698  = ~I... admit, when I saw you change, I wondered if we had truly lost, but then you found a way... somehow, you found the power to reclaim your body and mind. I knew, then, that nothing is lost yet. You have a power that Irenicus cannot notice, nor take away from you. Something much greater than what any one of us could have. Something that will be forever engraved upon your will.~
@699  = ~Erm... I don't really understand all this shamanic mumbo-jumbo, but... thank you, Will. We'll try our best. I hope that will be enough.~
@700  = ~I know myself. I know where my limits are, and I'm not even close to reaching them. Things will change if I make them. You'll see.~
@701  = ~Thanks for the kind words, Will.~
@702  = ~Whatever. Just give me a break so we can move on.~
@703  = ~We'll get your soul back or die trying. I know it'll be the former.~
@704  = ~Heh... I see. Irenicus may have stolen your soul, but... I guess no one could ever steal your confidence.~
@705  = ~Just one more thing... that creature that you turned into. You should be careful - I doubt shamanic sight would be necessary to know it is dangerous. Its claws can cleave through both the flesh and soul unlike any weapon could. So, again, I warn you... pleace, be careful.~
@706  = ~I will. But if I must become it, then I hope I can control it one day. Regardless, we should get moving.~
@707  = ~I only hope that I will have the strength to lock that power deep within me, so it may never surface again. Let's go.~
@708  = ~Let's just hope we'll never see that creature again. Come on, let's move.~
@709  = ~Aye, let's go.~
@710  = ~Hmm, I suppose you would prefer not to be bothered.~
@711  = ~I never expected to see a drow city with my own eyes. You can't deny that, even if the dark elves might be treacherous and vile, they have the talent to create things of beauty.~
@712  = ~I see no beauty. Only constructions as twisted as the beasts that built them.~
@713  = ~They do look rather interesting. I've never seen anything as... grandiose. Or spikey, for that matter. Yeesh.~
@714  = ~It's so horrible. I feel like I'm a small fry in the mouth of a shark.~
@715  = ~Now is neither the time nor the place for small talk. Come on, let's move.~
@716  = ~Well... you may be right. This architecture is rather disturbing in its wicked way, but... I just can't say it's bad. It's still a thing of art... with all the ways its creators played with its forms and shapes.~
@717  = ~Heh... I suppose that's an apt comparison, even if it's not one I would've thought of.~
@718  = ~I never considered the possibility of natural stones like stalagmites or stalagtites being shaped into actual homes, or for pits to be filled with such constructions.~
@719  = ~And as for the drow themselves, well... I never expected there to be so many of them in one place.~
@720  = ~That worries me the most. If we make one suspicious move, we'll be surrounded at all corners. We are totally, hopelessly outnumbered.~
@721  = ~We need to be careful. This is the lair of the spiders themselves. If we mess up, even slightly, we're dead.~
@722  = ~It's too risky to talk right now, Will. Let's move on before someone exposes us.~
@723  = ~Then we should act wisely and carefully. If we cannot kill them all, we should try not to. Perhaps we can survive this hell with no one being the wiser. After all we've been through, I'd hate for us to be slaughtered by drow now.~
@724  = ~Come, let's not make the suspicious.~
@725  = ~Perhaps you're right. We should get moving.~
@726  = ~It's good to see the light again. After all the time we spent travelling through Spellhold, then in the tunnels of the Underdark, I had missed this.~
@727  = ~I feel the same way. I was tired of all the danger, and the darkness, and the drow, and all the other monsters that dwell in the dark.~
@728  = ~There's hardly any difference. We may be back, but our situation hasn't gotten any better.~
@729  = ~We have no time to talk, Will. Our goal should be to stop our foes. They're too close to making their sick dreams come true.~
@730  = ~Well, I can't say we're done with fighting any more damned creatures, but at least it'll be under different circumstances.~
@731  = ~I think there is a difference. At least now we are once again walking the land we're familiar on, where we're safer. And our enemies - Bodhi and Irenicus - are running out of places to hide.~
@732  = ~I still wonder what traps Bodhi has planned for us. I have no doubt we'll be facing futher horrors. Irenicus is the mastermind, but Bodhi serves as his sharp fangs and deadly claws. It'd be too dangerous to let her get away once more, <CHARNAME>.~
@733  = ~Do you think I'd let that happen? If you, you still don't know me well enough, Will.~
@734  = ~I don't care what happens for her. I'll take what I need, and anything else isn't my business.~
@735  = ~She's been on my hit list for some time anyway. I know how dangerous she is. You don't need to tell me that she needs to be slain for the sake of the innocent.~
@736  = ~Can we find a better time to talk, Will? I'm too busy right now.~
@737  = ~I'm sorry for doubting you. I know you wouldn't simply let the beast get away.~
@738  = ~It's important, so please... please, think it over. You may defeat her, but unless you stop her for good, she will return. For you, and anyone else who stood against her. The risk is far too high not to setting things for good.~
@739  = ~Good... I'm relieved to hear that.~
@740  = ~As for the battle that is undoubtedly to come... I am well aware of Bodhi's great power, but... I may have a plan. This is dangerous, but... with my power, as well as that of the wisps and spirits that hear my calling, we may stand as a frontline against Bodhi's vampiric army. Her kind may drain the life of the living, but not mine. After all, I am dead as well.~
@741  = ~If you can ensure my safety, then I will unleash a legion of my faithful spirits against our enemy, and when the time is right, we may stab her in her black heart.~
@742  = ~Sounds like a plan.~
@743  = ~We'll see. I still need to think about the best possible plan.~
@744  = ~I'd rather just kill her with my own hands. I'm sure we're strong enough for that.~
@745  = ~I hope it'll be enough. We should prepare for the inevitable battle. Let's be sure we're truly ready for it.~
@746  = ~I understand. I trust in your leadership, <CHARNAME>, since you have led us this far. We should prepare for the inevitable battle. Let's be sure we're truly ready for it.~
@747  = ~I hope you're right about that. We should prepare for the inevitable battle. Let's be sure we're truly ready for it.~
@748  = ~Right... lead on. I'll be right behind you.~
@749  = ~So this is the famous elven city... I must say that it reminds me of the drow - Ust Natha, yes? It would be a pity to witness its fall. We need to stop Irenicus as soon as possible, <CHARNAME>. Let's go.~
@750  = ~Will Rattlemoth, the ghostly shaman who left the Visionhive to travel beside you, is looking back you with acceptance. He's supported you with all his power up till now, but you wonder if he is ready to risk his very existence for your sake.~
@751  = ~You've helped me so much, brother, but are you sure about following me in this? This may be truly dangerous. What if you cannot return to your grave this time?~
@752  = ~Are you ready for this, Will?~
@753  = ~You know, you don't have to come with me, if you don't want to...~
@754  = ~Heh, I want to go. I must help you. I would never forgive myself if I left you here, where you need my power. You'll need everything and everyone you've got to slay that monster Irenicus.~
@755  = ~No matter what's awaiting, I'm ready. Know that I'm with you. We'll finally end this once and for all.~
@756  = ~This is insanity. I can't believe this troll willingly caused all this destruction. Damn you, beast, I hope your soul rots in the Abyss!~
@757  = ~Hah! The puny ghost thinks to threaten TorGal? Weakling! TorGal fears not dead things like you!~
@758  = ~The land screams from the damage cause by her actions. I am surprised she cannot hear it, even though she is a druid.~
@759  = ~Wait, <CHARNAME>. I think... I have seen this man's thoughts, once. We should speak before we unleash our blades.~
@760  = ~Do you know her? Even if she is a drow, I can't agree to this gruesome display. Only the truly sick-minded would enjoy watching her flesh burn. Perhaps these men are the ones who truly deserve the stake.~
@761  = ~Sadness is engraved on this poor soul. We should listen to that boy, <CHARNAME>.~
@762  = ~Rest, child, you will find the peace you deserve. Listen to the whispers that call for you, and follow.~
@763  = ~I think I can... I can hear them...~
@764  = ~Watch out, <CHARNAME>. Men like this one always find themselves surrounded in blood and corpses.~
@765  = ~She is trying to provoke you with her words, <CHARNAME>. Watch out.~
@766  = ~Ha... do you really think you can see through my actions, little spectre? How pitiful. You should have remained at your little grotto for your own good.~
@767  = ~Why must mages always make their first words an insult to those they speak with?~
@768  = ~I do not think we should kill him, <CHARNAME>. No one would know if he were to just disappear instead.~
@769  = ~Is this all a game to him? Damn wyrm... I would see him dead, <CHARNAME>. His actions profaned this once peaceful land and turned it into a place of corruption.~
@770  = ~So- so many spirits speak of this woman... so many whispers, cursing, condemning her...~
@771  = ~I'm a bit surprised to see someone like this making his home in the sewers... assuming these are still the sewers.~
@772  = ~(whisper) <CHARNAME>, I think I might be falling in love with a beholder.~
@773  = ~Only an insane person would believe us to be sent by Sekolah.~
@774  = ~This--this creature is majestic! If it would help us, we may break Irenicus' forces!~
@775  = ~He must have used it in an even more vicious way - the spirits of the land are dying. They are losing to Irenicus and the otherworldly forces he has summoned. Their cries echo in my mind. We must make it stop.~
@776  = ~End this, Irenicus! Are you deaf to the pleading cries of the spirits? They scream so loudly, I can barely hear myself! STOP IT!~
@777  = ~I care nothing for the mewling of the dead, foolish ghost. You cannot presume to understand my actions! I will stop for nothing!~
@778  = ~That is so cruel...~
